          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. How an Oil-Filled Radiator Heater Works
          </h2>

          <p>
            The best oil-filled radiator heater is the one sized to your room with the safety features you need. Knowing how they work explains both their strengths and their limits.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Sealed Oil, Not Burning Oil</h3>

          <p>
            An electric element heats diathermic oil sealed inside the fins. The oil is never burned or used up; it is a heat reservoir. De'Longhi, Amazon Basics and COSTWAY all describe their oil as permanently sealed, so there is nothing to refill.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Heat That Lingers</h3>

          <p>
            Once the oil is hot, the fins keep releasing heat after the thermostat switches the element off. That is why radiator heaters feel steady and comfortable rather than blasting hot air in bursts.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">No Fan, No Noise</h3>

          <p>
            Most radiator heaters have no fan. They heat by radiation and gentle convection, so they are silent and do not blow dust around, which is why they are popular in bedrooms.
          </p>
        </div>

